<title>BELGIUM: Belgian money market supply raised in week.</title>
<headline>Belgian money market supply raised in week.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-05-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Belgian central bank said it</p>
<p>added liquidity to the money market in the week to May 12 to</p>
<p>offset a rise in notes in circulation.</p>
<p>(figures from the weekly statement in bln francs) -</p>
<p> Foreign currency reserves	   446.242 ( + 0.345)</p>
<p> Advances against pledged security  23.821 ( + 6.491)</p>
<p> Commercial bills			  2.546 ( + 0.031)</p>
<p> Securities portfolio		   25.794 ( + 1.985)</p>
<p> Money market interventions*	 106.113 ( - 4.618)</p>
<p> Bank notes in circulation	   473.794 ( - 4.618)</p>
<p>* comprises repurchase agreements and interbank loans</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
